\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab By the holy hills surrounded,
\par \pard\li720 On her firm base securely founded,
\par Stands fast the city of the Lord :
\par None shall rend her walls asunder ;
\par On her men look with fear and wonder,
\par And mark who here keeps watch and ward.
\par He slumbers not, nor sleeps,
\par Who His loved Israel keeps.
\par Hallelujah !
\par Who through God's grace
\par Shall have in her their dwelling-place !
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab Zion's gates Jehovah loveth,
\par \pard\fi360\li360 and with especial grace approveth ;
\par he maketh fast her bolts and bars ;
\par those who dwell in her He blesses,
\par and comforts them in their distresses
\par who cast on Him their griefs and cares.
\par How wonderful the grace 
\par With which He doth embrace
\par All his people !
\par City of God,
\par How sweet the abode
\par On which such blessings are bestowed !
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab Taught in thee is a salvation
\par \pard\fi360\li360 Unknown to every other nation ;
\par There great and holy things are heard ;
\par In the midst of thee abiding,
\par Enlightening, comforting, and guiding,
\par Thou hast the spirit and the Word ;
\par There breathing peace around
\par Is heard the joyful sound,
\par Grace and mercy !
\par how sweet that is,
\par Which here speaks peace,
\par There crowns with everlasting bliss.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

